# TEMPLATE ONLY - staging. Standalone Selenium CLI needs no database or LLM keys.
# Run CLI with --mode selenium explicitly; default CLI mode is browser-use.
# Browser mode, limits and output directory are CLI/job parameters, not env keys.
# Keep output/checkpoint storage persistent and separate for staging.
# Dynamic keywords/portals/schedules belong to backend workflow configuration.
# Integrated worker: Compose reads DATABASE_URL and runtime settings from the
# matching backend .env.staging selected with --env-file. The backend worker owns
# the PostgreSQL queue; no crawler HTTP service is used. APP_ENV is read by that
# worker. Never copy Supabase API keys or Browser Use provider keys into its image.
# See specs-careeros/ENVIRONMENT_VARIABLES.md.

# Shared global execution capacity; replicate workers separately for parallel runs.
CRAWLER_MAX_CONCURRENCY=1
# Compose only: independent worker processes, one browser/run per replica.
# Set this AND CRAWLER_MAX_CONCURRENCY in the BACKEND env passed to Compose.
CRAWLER_WORKER_REPLICAS=1
